    This is the literal reading of your request, and I'd push back on it: a client-supplied identity that the auth path
    trusts is the shape of an auth bypass. It only makes sense if some upstream system already authenticated the user
    and this stub is downstream of that — which isn't the case in this repo today.

  [1mMy recommendation: the first.[0m It's the only one that actually answers "who logged in" with a trustworthy value, and it
  doesn't change the signature other code depends on. If you also want failed attempts traceable, the correlation ID
  composes with it — they aren't exclusive.

